---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HorizontalCard from '../components/HorizontalCard.astro';
import UnhurriedArchitecture from '../components/UnhurriedArchitecture.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Projects & Systems"
  description="Curated technical projects, cloud architecture blueprints, forensics investigations, and engineering research by Ishfaque Jahan Rafee."
  sideBarActiveItemID="projects"
>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Projects &amp; Systems</h1>
    <p class="text-base sm:text-lg opacity-80 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      A curated overview of active systems engineering projects, cloud security blueprints, enterprise Zero-Trust architectures, and open-source contributions.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Flagship Section: Unhurried -->
  <section id="unhurried" class="mb-12">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
      <div>
        <span class="badge badge-primary badge-outline text-xs uppercase font-mono tracking-wider mb-1">
          Flagship Systems Project
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Unhurried — The Intentional Career Platform
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <a
          href="https://unhurried-careers.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="badge badge-ghost gap-1 py-3 px-3 hover:scale-105 transition-transform font-mono"
        >
          <span>Live Web App</span>
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 3h7v7h-2V6.414l-9.293 9.293-1.414-1.414L17.586 5H14V3zM5 5h6V3H5c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v14c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2v-6h-2v6H5V5z"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Unhurried-Careers"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="badge badge-primary gap-1 py-3 px-3 hover:scale-105 transition-transform font-mono"
        >
          <span>GitHub Org</span>
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 3h7v7h-2V6.414l-9.293 9.293-1.414-1.414L17.586 5H14V3zM5 5h6V3H5c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v14c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2v-6h-2v6H5V5z"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Product Motivation & Philosophy -->
    <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm mb-6">
      <div class="prose max-w-none text-base">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-base-content mt-0 mb-3">Breaking the AI Auto-Apply Noise Loop</h3>
        <p>
          AI-driven auto-apply tools have created an absurd loop across modern hiring: AI writes the job descriptions, AI mass-applies with customized resumes, AI screens submissions, and AI rejects candidates before any human ever reviews the application. Job seekers are forced to "spray and pray" across dozens of boards, while hiring teams are overwhelmed by thousands of low-signal submissions.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Unhurried</strong> fundamentally slows down the process. Instead of treating AI as a spam cannon, Unhurried treats AI as a <strong>diligent personal researcher</strong>. It enforces deliberate decision-making: candidates specify target companies, roles, and dealbreaker requirements with documented written rationale before discovering matching postings.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-base-content mt-6 mb-3">Core Operating Principles &amp; Hard Gates</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Direction Before Postings:</strong> Users establish target companies and target roles—each with a mandatory written reason—plus must-haves and dealbreaker requirements evaluated against evidence before deciding to apply.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Strict $\le 5$ Active Shortlist Ceiling:</strong> The pipeline enforces a server-side hard ceiling of at most <strong>5 active opportunities</strong> across the <code>decided</code> and <code>tailored</code> stages. Every stage transition (<em>Considering &rarr; Researching &rarr; Decided &rarr; Tailored &rarr; Applied</em>) requires a written rationale (&ge; 30 characters) to pass the gate.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Intentional Outreach Kit:</strong> Rather than transactional referral requests, the system generates targeted LinkedIn search links, thoughtful connection notes (&le; 300 characters), follow-ups, and interview inquiry questions geared toward curious, peer-to-peer conversations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Resume Studio (Google Docs Workspace):</strong> Seamlessly links with Google Drive via the <code>drive.file</code> scope using Google Picker, creating and tailoring Google Doc resumes to shortlisted role criteria via <strong>Vertex AI (Gemini 3.5 Flash)</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Apply Assistant, Never an Automaton:</strong> A companion Chrome Manifest V3 extension talks strictly via <code>window.postMessage</code> relay to the authenticated web app. It pre-fills ATS forms (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workday) but strictly requires the user's manual review and confirmation (<code>confirmed: true</code>)—it <strong>never</strong> auto-submits.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Calendar &amp; Interview Intelligence:</strong> Integrates with the Google Calendar API (<code>calendar.events.readonly</code> scope), using deterministic heuristics to detect interview rounds and calculate free availability slots without persistently storing user calendar events.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Live Architecture Blueprint -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <UnhurriedArchitecture />
    </div>

    <!-- 10 Repositories Microservices Architecture Breakdown -->
    <div class="mb-10">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Microservices &amp; Multi-Repository Breakdown</h3>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-80 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
        The system is partitioned into 10 purpose-built repositories within the <a href="https://github.com/Unhurried-Careers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Unhurried-Careers</a> GitHub organization. Go backend services run containerized on Google Cloud Run (Go 1.27, Distroless nonroot), scaling to zero when idle.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <!-- unhurried-web -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-web</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">React 18 / TypeScript</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Single-page app deployed on Firebase Hosting Global CDN (<code>unhurried-careers.com</code>). Features a step-by-step pipeline stepper, Direction &amp; Research dashboard, Google Picker integration, and conversation timelines.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Vite &bull; Tailwind CSS &bull; Firebase Auth &bull; App Check</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-extension -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-extension</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Chrome MV3</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Client-side apply assistant communicating solely through <code>window.postMessage</code> with the signed-in web tab. Detects ATS form fields (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workday), pre-fills applicant data, and holds zero tokens.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Manifest V3 &bull; Content Script &bull; Zero Credentials</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-common -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-common</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Go Shared Library</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Core hardening library imported across all Go services. Implements hand-rolled RS256 token verification, App Check validation, Google OIDC internal token verification, HTTP recovery, request timeouts, and domain models.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">RS256 JWT &bull; App Check &bull; Allowlist &bull; Field Validation</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-job-search -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-job-search</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Go / Cloud Run</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Two entry pathways: search open roles across Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, and Adzuna, or paste a posting URL (anti-SSRF safe fetcher). Company lookups (Clearbit autocomplete + Wikidata), roles (ESCO + Wikidata), and grounded research summaries with Google Search citations via <strong>Vertex AI (Gemini 3.5 Flash)</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Cloud Run &bull; Vertex AI Gemini &bull; Board APIs &bull; Anti-SSRF</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-applications -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-applications</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Go / Cloud Run</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Enforces the 5-stage gate pipeline (Reason &ge; 30 chars, evidence &ge; 10 chars), the hard &le; 5 shortlist ceiling across <code>decided</code>/<code>tailored</code>, generates personalized Outreach Kits (&le; 300-char notes, LinkedIn search links), and tracks interview rounds.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Cloud Run &bull; Stage Gate Machine &bull; Outreach Generator</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-resume -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-resume</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Go / Cloud Run</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Integrates with Google Docs &amp; Drive (<code>drive.file</code> scope). Master resumes picked via Google Picker are copied into the "Unhurried resumes" folder (original untouched). Generates per-opportunity copies tailored via Gemini 3.5 Flash under strict Honesty Rules, applying atomic text replacements.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Google Drive API &bull; Vertex AI &bull; Cloud KMS Encryption</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-inbox -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-inbox</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Go / Cloud Run</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Queries Google Calendar (<code>calendar.events.readonly</code> scope) live (past/next 60 days) to match likely interviews against applied rounds without storing calendar events in Firestore. Outreach booking pages are user-provided via Google Calendar appointment links (verified clipboard integration).
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Google Calendar API &bull; KMS Decryption &bull; Live Event Heuristics</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-notifications -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-notifications</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Go / Cloud Run</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Triggered by Cloud Scheduler and internal job-search scans to generate and dispatch daily job discovery digests matching the user's direction via Resend SMTP relay.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Resend SMTP &bull; Cloud Scheduler &bull; OIDC Internal Auth</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-infra -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-infra</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Terraform IaC</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Complete declarative infrastructure for GCP: 5 Google API Gateways with OpenAPI 2.0 specs, Cloud Run services, Cloud KMS key rings, Secret Manager secrets, and fine-grained IAM service accounts.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Terraform &bull; GCP API Gateway &bull; KMS &bull; Cloud Run</div>
        </div>

        <!-- unhurried-product -->
        <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-5 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-primary/40 transition-colors">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono font-bold text-primary">unhurried-product</span>
            <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm font-mono">Documentation</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm opacity-85 mb-3">
            Comprehensive product reasoning, architectural diagrams, threat model, security controls matrix, CI/CD operational runbooks, and implementation status documentation.
          </p>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono opacity-60">Markdown &bull; Threat Model &bull; Architecture Specs</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Security Architecture & Fail-Closed Defense -->
    <div class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-base-content mb-3">Multi-Layered Fail-Closed Security Architecture</h3>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-85 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        As a security engineer, Unhurried was architected with defense-in-depth where every tier fails closed and validates inputs independently:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
        <div class="p-4 bg-base-200/50 rounded-xl border border-base-300/60">
          <div class="font-bold font-mono text-primary mb-1">1. Edge &amp; API Gateway Defense</div>
          <p class="opacity-80 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            API Keys restricted to website referrers, per-minute rate-limit quotas (300 req/min per service), App Check attestation via reCAPTCHA Enterprise, and RS256 Firebase ID token signature validation at the gateway edge.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-base-200/50 rounded-xl border border-base-300/60">
          <div class="font-bold font-mono text-primary mb-1">2. Zero-Trust Go Middleware Re-Verification</div>
          <p class="opacity-80 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            <code>unhurried-common</code> never blindly trusts edge proxies. It re-verifies RS256 token signatures against Google public keys, enforces a strict email allowlist (<code>ALLOWED_EMAILS</code>), and validates strict body limits (1 MiB max).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-base-200/50 rounded-xl border border-base-300/60">
          <div class="font-bold font-mono text-primary mb-1">3. Cryptographic Token Sealing (Cloud KMS)</div>
          <p class="opacity-80 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Sensitive third-party OAuth refresh tokens (Google Calendar and Google Drive) are envelope-encrypted using Cloud KMS key ring <code>unhurried</code> before writing to Cloud Firestore. Raw tokens are never stored in plaintext.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-base-200/50 rounded-xl border border-base-300/60">
          <div class="font-bold font-mono text-primary mb-1">4. Anti-SSRF Socket Protections</div>
          <p class="opacity-80 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Link fetching in <code>job-search</code> strictly validates resolved socket addresses post-DNS resolution, rejecting loopback, private, link-local (GCP metadata server <code>169.254.169.254</code>), and shared/reserved IP ranges with zero proxy fallback.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-base-200/50 rounded-xl border border-base-300/60">
          <div class="font-bold font-mono text-primary mb-1">5. Internal Service-to-Service OIDC Mesh</div>
          <p class="opacity-80 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Inter-service calls on <code>/internal/*</code> are never published on API Gateway. They require Google-signed OIDC bearer tokens with audience <code>unhurried-internal</code> and an explicit caller service account whitelist.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-base-200/50 rounded-xl border border-base-300/60">
          <div class="font-bold font-mono text-primary mb-1">6. Zero-GCP CI &amp; SLSA Verified CD Pipeline</div>
          <p class="opacity-80 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            Work flows <code>dev &rarr; staging &rarr; main</code> across all 10 repositories. GitHub Actions executes pure read-only CI without cloud credentials (gofmt, race tests, govulncheck binary scanning, and Vitest). Google Cloud Build and Cloud Deploy create immutable releases with custom target type <code>cloud-run-image</code> and SLSA-verified provenance in Artifact Registry, supporting one-click rollbacks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider my-8"></div>

  <!-- Enterprise Security & Cloud Defense Systems -->
  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">
      Enterprise Security Architecture &amp; Engineering Systems
    </h2>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <HorizontalCard
        title="Zero-Trust Network Access & SASE Architecture"
        desc="Designed and implemented enterprise-wide SASE and ZTNA using Cloudflare One, paired with Microsoft Entra ID conditional access and phishing-resistant FIDO2 MFA for identity-centric perimeters."
        url="/about/"
        badge="ZERO TRUST"
        tags={["Cloudflare One", "ZTNA", "Entra ID", "SASE", "MFA"]}
      />

      <HorizontalCard
        title="Competitive Platform Proof-of-Value (PoV) Program"
        desc="Technical validation assessments benchmarking Palo Alto Networks, SentinelOne, and CrowdStrike across enterprise workloads, driving $200K CAD in annual savings and 45% budget efficiency."
        url="/about/"
        badge="PoV / ARCHITECTURE"
        tags={["CrowdStrike", "SentinelOne", "Palo Alto", "EDR", "SIEM"]}
      />

      <HorizontalCard
        title="Dynamic Application Security Testing (DAST) Program"
        desc="Evaluated 7 DAST platforms and deployed Escape DAST with Jira automated remediation pipelines, transitioning to risk-based traffic scoring and eliminating 100% of WAF exceptions."
        url="/about/"
        badge="APPSEC"
        tags={["DAST", "Escape", "AppSec", "WAF", "API Security"]}
      />

      <HorizontalCard
        title="DFIR Memory Forensics Automation Pipeline"
        desc="Reproducible incident response workflows built on top of Volatility 3 and custom python parsers for identifying process injection, unlinked DLLs, and rogue C2 beacons in memory dumps."
        url="/posts/htb_recollection/"
        badge="FORENSICS"
        tags={["DFIR", "Volatility3", "Memory Forensics", "Incident Response"]}
      />

      <HorizontalCard
        title="Multi-Cloud Governance & Automated Change Management"
        desc="Multi-cloud guardrails across AWS, Azure, and OCI leveraging AWS Control Tower for SOC2 and ISO 27001/42001 compliance, plus custom Python API automations cutting operational overhead by 70%."
        url="/posts/iac/"
        badge="AUTOMATION"
        tags={["AWS Control Tower", "Python", "SOC2", "ISO 27001", "IaC"]}
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
